# Build output from the host machine.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` drags the developer's bin/ and obj/ into the Linux image —
# including obj/project.assets.json, which contains absolute Windows paths like
# C:\Users\...\.nuget\packages. That silently overwrites the assets file produced by the
# restore layer, so the publish either rebuilds from scratch (throwing away the cache) or
# fails outright once --no-restore is used.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/

# Never bake real credentials into an image layer. .env.example is kept deliberately.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not needed to build, and .git in particular is large and changes every commit, which
# would bust the Docker layer cache on every push.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# Test project — the runtime image restores and publishes Auth.API only. Excluding it here
# means adding another test or tooling project can never affect the deploy.
Auth.Tests/

# Documentation and local tooling.
docs/
*.md
docker-compose.yml
